    {
      "bbox": [
        562,
        1212,
        1993,
        1648
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, the Charter of the City of New York empowers the Mayor to create or abolish, by Executive Order, bureaus, divisions or positions within the executive office of the Mayor as he may find necessary to fulfill his duties and may from time to time, by Executive Order, delegate to or withdraw from any member of said office, specified functions, powers and duties, except his power to act on local laws or resolutions of the Council, to act as a magistrate or to appoint or remove officials:",
